      "PostedDate": "2026-09-25T18:47:40.409Z",
      "BriefDescription": "The Embedded Software Engineer designs, develops, and supports Wi-Fi radio firmware and driver software for Ezurio's wireless connectivity products, working closely with the RF hardware development team in the USA and Taiwan, program management, and customers to deliver reliable, innovative, and resilient embedded software. The ideal candidate is comfortable working close to the metal - register-level access, bootloaders, and drivers in a resource-constrained environment - as well as building the connectivity stacks that sit above them, and brings strong debugging and root-cause analysis skills to complex hardware/software and RF interaction issues. Deep 802.11 protocol expertise is not required; we are willing to train a strong embedded/RTOS candidate on the Wi-Fi-specific pieces.",
